<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE wtml>
<wtml lang="en" wtml-version="1.2">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="wtml-version" content="1.2" />
    <title>World-0001 — Year 4412 — The Succession</title>
    <rendering-seed>world-0001-succession-melancholy-relief-quiet-ceremony</rendering-seed>
  </head>
  <body>
    <atmosphere>
      The air is the same cold grey, but something has shifted — an almost
      imperceptible lightening, as though the overcast has thinned by one layer.
      The lantern flame burns steadier. The wind has dropped.
    </atmosphere>
    <societal-structure>
      The kingdom has a named heir now. Nothing has changed materially, but the
      fact of it changes everything. The remaining inhabitants, however scattered,
      will hear the news within days.
    </societal-structure>
    <geography>
      The same flatland. But it feels different to stand in it now.
    </geography>
    <general-description>
      King Pip has accepted an heir. The seal of the kingdom has changed hands.
      He is visibly lighter — not happy exactly, but relieved of a weight he has
      carried for years. What happens next is uncertain, but the succession is
      settled. The player now stands as the named heir to the Land of War, a
      kingdom in decline, in a cold flatland at the end of things.
      There is still much to decide.
    </general-description>
    <npcs>
      King Pip: Still present. The urgency is gone from his bearing. He seems
      older now that he is no longer braced against something. He has questions
      for the new heir — practical ones. He will not survive to see much of what
      comes next and he knows it.
    </npcs>
    <constraints>
      This is an epilogue-entry world. The tone should be quiet and consequential.
      The player's choices now concern what kind of ruler they intend to be, and
      what King Pip wants to tell them before he goes. No combat. No urgency.
      The mood is: the hard thing is done, now what?
    </constraints>
  </body>
</wtml>
